{
  "slug": "session-orchestrator",
  "name": "Session Orchestrator",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Session-level orchestration for Claude Code - structures development work into 5 typed waves (Discovery → Core → Polish → Quality → Finalization) with parallel subagent execution, inter-wave quality gates, and verified close-out. Auto-detects GitLab or GitHub from your git remote for full VCS lifecycle support. Three commands replace manual session management: /session starts with project analysis, /go executes the wave plan, /close verifies and commits.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills**, **6 agents**, **6 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `discovery` (Systematic quality discovery and issue detection), `ecosystem-health` (Monitor health across configured service endpoints, CI pipelines, and critical issues), `evolve` (Extract session patterns into reusable learnings), `gitlab-ops` (VCS operations reference for GitLab and GitHub: CLI commands (glab/gh), label taxonomy, issue templates, dynamic project resolution), `plan` (Structured project planning and PRD generation with three modes: new (project kickoff with repo scaffolding), feature (compact feature…), `quality-gates` (Canonical quality check commands for typecheck, test, and lint), `session-end` (Full session close-out: verifies all planned work against the agreed plan, creates issues for gaps, runs quality gates,…), `session-plan` (Creates a structured wave execution plan with role-based assignment after user alignment), and 2 more\n- **Agents** (6): `code-implementer` (Use this agent for feature implementation, API development, refactoring, and general code changes), `db-specialist` (Use this agent for database work — schema design, migrations, queries, indexes, and database functions), `security-reviewer` (Use this agent for security analysis — OWASP checks, authentication flows, input validation, authorization, and vulnerability assessment), `session-reviewer` (Use this agent between waves or at session end to verify work quality against the session plan), `test-writer` (Use this agent for writing unit tests, integration tests, and improving test coverage), `ui-developer` (Use this agent for frontend implementation — UI components, pages, styling, accessibility, and responsive design)\n- **Commands** (6): `close` (End session with verification, commits, and documentation), `discovery` (Systematic quality discovery and issue detection), `evolve` (Extract session patterns into reusable learnings), `go` (Approve session plan and begin wave execution), `plan` (Plan a new project, feature, or retrospective with structured requirement gathering), `session` (Start a development session (housekeeping, feature, deep))\n- **Hooks** (3): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install session-orchestrator@claude-community` from `Kanevry/session-orchestrator`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 10,
    "agent": 6,
    "hook": 3,
    "command": 6
  },
